<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2462" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănăthĕmătīzo</span></b> ,
			āre, v. a., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναθεματίζω</span>.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to anathematize</i>,
				<i>to put under the ban</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem or aliquam rem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug.
					Ep. 75</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gen., <i>to curse</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Macc.
				5, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">ib. Marc. 14,
			71</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>To detest</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 75</span></i>
			.—Form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănă-thĕmo</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Aug.
				Serm. 164</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Temp. 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ep.
			95</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>